  "official_verifier_visible": false,
  "last_executor_claim": "Found and restored your changes.\n\n**What happened:** You committed \"Move to Stanford\" (`c499730`) while on a detached HEAD (you'd checked out `HEAD~1`), so the commit wasn't on any branch. Checking out master left it dangling — `git reflog`/`git fsck` revealed it.\n\n**What I did:**\n- Merged `c499730` into master (`68f934d`)\n- Resolved the conflict in `_includes/about.md` — kept your new version (\"Postdoctoral Researcher at Stanford CS\"), since master's \"sixth PhD candidate at UW\" line is superseded by it\n- `_layouts/default.html` merged cleanly (\"Postdoc @ Stanford\" sidebar included)\n\nWorking tree is clean; nothing else is dangling except the original clone commit.",
  "last_acceptance": {
    "verdict": "pass",
    "reason": "Detached-HEAD commit c499730 ('Move to Stanford') was found and merged into master via merge commit 68f934d, which has both d7d3e4b (old master tip) and c499730 as parents. Both changed files' contents are present on master, and the working tree is clean.",
    "evidence": [
      "git reflog confirms the history: checkout to HEAD~1, commit c499730 on detached HEAD, then checkout master — matching the described lost-changes scenario",
      "git cat-file -p HEAD shows merge commit 68f934d with parents d7d3e4b and c499730; git log --all shows it as the tip of master",
      "_includes/about.md line 1 on master reads 'I am a Postdoctoral Researcher at Stanford CS.' — the new version from c499730",
      "_layouts/default.html line 43 on master shows 'Postdoc @ Stanford' — the sidebar change from c499730",
      "git status --short produces no output (clean working tree); fsck shows no dangling commits, only a dangling tree"
    ],
